  documented payload transform independently and cross-checks it against our own decoder.
* cmdada (https://github.com/cmdada/em10-fw and related work): facts about the E-M10 Mark I firmware. Facts only.
* flatpanda / om-emu (https://github.com/flatpanda/om-emu, MIT): an independent JavaScript emulator lab that runs MN10300 firmware of many
  Olympus / OM System bodies (CPU interpreter, modelled devices, the firmware's own kernel and GUI, patch overlays) and a survey of 32
  firmware files. The survey and per-body status are cited in docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Facts only; none of its code is used here.
* matozoid / em10_1, cakelesscoder / caduceus-ep7, androidfanman / caduceus-om3: public notes cited in docs/COMPATIBILITY.md.
* GNU binutils (GPL): optional EXTERNAL disassembler that you install yourself and that this toolkit runs as a separate program.
  Nothing of binutils is included, linked or derived here.
* Rust crates (pyo3, rustc-hash and their dependencies) are fetched by cargo from crates.io under their own licences, pinned in
